  "raw_label": "appellant_lost",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "N.Kamaraj vs The Food Safety Officer on 10 June, 2024 Crl.O.P.(MD) N Before The Madurai Bench Of Madras High Court Dated: 10.06.2024 Coram The Honourable Mr. Justice A.A.Nakkiran Crl.O.P (Md) No.2865 of 2021 and Crl.M.P(MD) Nos.1529 & 1530 of 2021 1. N.Kamaraj 2. M.Prabhakaran ... Petitioners/Accused N Vs The Food Safety Officer, Madurai Corporation ( Code No.572), Food Safety and Drug Administration Department, Viswanathapuram, Madurai-625 014. ... Respondent /Complainant PRAYER: Criminal Original Petition filed under Section 482 of Cr.P. praying to call for records and quash the proceedings in S.T.C.No.3 2020 on the file of the Judicial Magistrate Court No.1, Madurai aga petitioners. For Petitioners : Mr.M.Rajaraman For Respondent : Mr.R.M.Anbunithi Additional Public Prosecuto 1/8 https://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis Crl.O.P.(MD) ORDER N.Kamaraj vs The Food Safety Officer on 10 June, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/175089007/ 1 2.",
    "facts": "The Food Analyst had sent a report on 11.03.2020 stating that the sample was substandard and unsafe. sought for permission to initiate proceedings against the accused. Since there was no claim from the petitioners to sent the second sample for analyzing, a complaint was lodged before the learned Judicial Magistrate Court No.I, Madurai as per Section 190(1)(a) and 200 of Cr.P.C., against the accused for the offences punishable under Sections 51, 59(i) of the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006 and the same was taken on file in S.T.C.No.3550 of 2020. Due to Covid-19 pandemic, the Government has announced lock down from 23.03.2020 and there was no opportunity to the petitioners to file an appeal. Based on that only, the present proceedings have been initiated against the petitioners.",
    "arguments": "He further submitted that there are materials available to proceed with the case as against the petitioners herein and at the threshold, the criminal proceedings cannot be [LEAKAGE_MASK] and the charges against the petitioners have to be gone into only at the time of trial and hence, he prayed for dismissal of the petition."
  },
